WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:12.959
Today is a historic day for Croatia
and for the European Union.

00:00:13.125 --> 00:00:18.209
Nearly nine years since
you applied for membership,

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:21.000
after six years of negotiations,

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:24.292
the Accession Treaty of Croatia
to the European Union

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:27.042
is ready for signature.

00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:33.375
Croatia is set to become
the 28th Member State of the Union.

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:38.834
Welcome to the European Union!

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:44.250
The signing ceremony was
the crowning of a very long process

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:47.250
that started on 3rd October 2005.

00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.999
It took a number of years to accomplish,

00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:54.918
so, finally, when the signatures
were put on our Accession Treaty,

00:00:55.042 --> 00:01:03.292
that was symbolically and practically
the end of a very, very long process.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:26.375
After the Accession Treaty is signed you
acquire the status of permanent observer

00:01:26.542 --> 00:01:31.626
and you can participate
in almost all the working bodies

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:37.250
and the Councils, all the ministerial
meetings and European Council meetings,

00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:42.209
and, of course, the world of the Council
is now fully open to you.

00:01:45.542 --> 00:01:51.626
It has been an extremely beneficial
and fantastic experience

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:55.959
to be able to sit in the meetings
of the Foreign Affairs Council

00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.417
and the meetings
of the General Affairs Council.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:02.417
Also my colleagues are
in those of Ecofin

00:02:02.584 --> 00:02:06.626
and the Agricultural Ministers Council

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:12.751
and, of course, the Prime Minister is
in the meetings of the European Council.

00:02:12.918 --> 00:02:17.292
Although we don't have a vote
until we are full members,

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:19.083
we have everything else,

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:22.834
we have the possibility of hearing
what people are saying,

00:02:22.999 --> 00:02:26.792
we have the possibility of being here
when decisions are being made,

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:29.792
we have the possibility
of debating and discussing

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:33.709
and expressing our opinions
the same as everybody else.

00:02:41.876 --> 00:02:45.542
With every enlargement we need new staff
to come and work for the EU,

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:49.459
so in view of the upcoming accession
of Croatia to the EU,

00:02:49.626 --> 00:02:53.667
the European Personnel Selection Office
last summer started

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.709
selection of Croatian staff
in different fields.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.167
We are running selection procedures
for general administrators,

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:03.375
for translators and interpreters,
and for assistants

00:03:03.584 --> 00:03:07.375
in the field of project management,
law and communication.

00:03:07.542 --> 00:03:13.042
By 1st July we will have selected
about 360 Croatian staff

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:15.292
to come and work for
the EU institutions.

00:03:20.792 --> 00:03:25.751
The Council prepared well
for Croatia's accession

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:32.042
and creation of the new unit
started a year before Croatia joined.

00:03:32.792 --> 00:03:37.999
Croatia entering the EU
is a big thing in our country

00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:43.751
and us being here is really exciting,
taking part in the whole process.

00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:48.459
It is a very good feeling
that our language

00:03:48.626 --> 00:03:53.375
is now part of the family of languages
here at the Council

00:03:53.542 --> 00:03:58.959
and that the Croatian language will
now be the 24th language of the EU.

00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:01.709
It is a great honour
and it is very exciting

00:04:01.876 --> 00:04:08.626
to feel part of
the whole project of the EU.

00:04:16.584 --> 00:04:20.000
When Croatia got candidate status
and we started accession talks,

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:24.167
the number of journalists grew,
there are between 8 and 10.

00:04:26.876 --> 00:04:31.834
I travel from Zagreb to Brussels
once a month, sometimes more often,

00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:35.292
but when we become a member
of the European Union,

00:04:35.459 --> 00:04:37.792
Brussels will be our second capital.

00:04:40.209 --> 00:04:44.334
Institutions are adapting to the fact
that we, as Croatian journalists,

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:51.709
are here and we have questions that
are not only about enlargement anymore,

00:04:51.876 --> 00:04:57.042
but about all the different issues
and portfolios.

00:04:57.209 --> 00:04:59.834
Our hopes for the future
are high, of course.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:04.709
For a couple of hours on 1st July
we are first going to enjoy

00:05:04.876 --> 00:05:07.209
the beauty and the miracle
of our membership,

00:05:07.375 --> 00:05:11.792
then it's back to the hard work,
because the work in the EU never ends.

00:05:11.959 --> 00:05:14.999
We really do feel at home
around the Council tables

00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:17.918
and it's a very, very good feeling.

